@startuml Assignment Sequence

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor DarkBlue
    ActorBorderColor DarkBlue
    LifeLineBorderColor DarkBlue
    ParticipantBackgroundColor LightBlue
    ParticipantBorderColor DarkBlue
}

title User Assignment Flow (Repository Pattern)

actor Client
participant "Router\n(experiments.py)" as Router
participant "Auth" as Auth
participant "Cache" as Cache
participant "ExperimentRepository\n(interface)" as Repo
participant "SQLAlchemy\nImplementation" as Impl
database "SQLite" as DB

== First Request ==

Client -> Router : GET /experiments/{id}/assignment/{user_id}\n[Authorization: Bearer token]
Router -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> Router : Token valid

Router -> Cache : Check cache\nkey: "assignment:{id}:{user_id}"
Cache --> Router : Cache miss

Router -> Repo : get_by_id(experiment_id)
Repo -> Impl : get_by_id()
Impl -> DB : SELECT experiment
DB --> Impl : Experiment data
Impl --> Repo : ExperimentEntity
Repo --> Router : ExperimentEntity

Router -> Repo : get_assignment(experiment_id, user_id)
Repo -> Impl : get_assignment()
Impl -> DB : SELECT assignment
DB --> Impl : Not found
Impl --> Repo : None
Repo --> Router : None

Router -> Repo : get_variants(experiment_id)
Repo -> Impl : get_variants()
Impl -> DB : SELECT variants
DB --> Impl : Variants list
Impl --> Repo : list[VariantEntity]
Repo --> Router : list[VariantEntity]

Router -> Router : Calculate weighted\nrandom selection

Router -> Repo : create_assignment(experiment_id, variant_id, user_id)
Repo -> Impl : create_assignment()
Impl -> DB : INSERT assignment
DB --> Impl : Created
Impl --> Repo : AssignmentEntity
Repo --> Router : AssignmentEntity

Router -> Cache : Store in cache (TTL: 5min)
Cache --> Router : Cached

Router --> Client : 200 OK\n{"variant_name": "Control", ...}

== Subsequent Request (Same User) ==

Client -> Router : GET /experiments/{id}/assignment/{user_id}\n[Authorization: Bearer token]
Router -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> Router : Token valid

Router -> Cache : Check cache\nkey: "assignment:{id}:{user_id}"
Cache --> Router : Cache hit!

Router --> Client : 200 OK\n{"variant_name": "Control", ...}\n(Same assignment - Idempotent)

note right of Repo
  **Repository Pattern:**
  Router depends on
  abstract interface,
  not SQLAlchemy directly
end note

note right of Cache
  Cache ensures fast
  subsequent requests
  and guarantees
  idempotency
end note

@enduml
